# vvaharness/validation/claude_config/hooks/logging/capture_transcript.sh

Stop hook copied into the validation workspace's `.claude/hooks/logging/`. When an operator opts in, it copies the raw (unredacted) Claude session transcript into the session log directory. It fails open: every failure exits 0.

Source: `vvaharness/validation/claude_config/hooks/logging/capture_transcript.sh` (lines 1-35)
Executor: code
Called from: the Claude Code Stop hook declared in `vvaharness/validation/claude_config/settings.sudo.md` (installed by `vvaharness/validation/session/config_inject.sudo`)

// src: vvaharness/validation/claude_config/hooks/logging/capture_transcript.sh:16-35
fn capture_transcript(hook_input_on_stdin):executor=code {
  // "The raw transcript is UNREDACTED ... Persist it only when an operator explicitly opts in for debugging"
  require environment VALIDATION_DEBUG_TRANSCRIPT is non-empty => exit 0   // default: nothing is written
  transcript = hook_input.transcript_path (leading "~" expanded to $HOME), or "" when jq fails
  log_dir = environment VALIDATION_LOG_DIR or ""
  require transcript is non-empty && transcript is a file && log_dir is non-empty => exit 0
  copy transcript to "$log_dir/subagents/transcript.jsonl" (creating the directory; errors ignored)
  exit 0
}
// external: jq parses the hook input
